data: {"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"He picked the third option, which was correct, so on this question the evaluation point is checked honestly. Next, I'm checking the \"why multiply\" idea again with the correct answer in a different position."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_011MwUAGD7o5xVCaVdf9F1Qo","name":"probe","arguments":{"question":"In $h'(x) = f'(g(x))\\cdot g'(x)$, why is $f'$ evaluated at $g(x)$ rather than at $x$?","options":[{"label":"Because $f'$ must be evaluated at the same point as $g'$ so the two rates are comparable","value":"same"},{"label":"Because the chain rule formula is defined that way, and evaluating at $x$ would give the derivative of $f(x)$ instead","value":"defn"},{"label":"Because $g(x)$ is larger than $x$, so the outer function changes faster there","value":"larger"},{"label":"Because $f$ only ever receives $g(x)$ as its input, so its local rate of change matters at that input, not at $x$","value":"input"}],"explanation":"$f$ never sees $x$. It only receives whatever $g$ outputs. When $x$ is nudged, $g(x)$ moves, and how strongly $f$ responds depends on $f$'s slope at the point where it is actually operating, which is $g(x)$. For example, $f'(x)$ would be the rate of $f$ near $x$, a place $f$ isn't even being used.\n- The two rates are *not* at the same point. $g'$ is taken at $x$ and $f'$ at $g(x)$, because each function is used at a different input.\n- \"Defined that way\" is circular. It describes the formula without explaining it.\n- Whether $g(x)$ is larger than $x$ is irrelevant. It could be smaller.","correctAnswer":"input"}}],"api":"claude-code-cli","provider":"claude-code","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":992,"cacheRead":9460,"cacheWrite":7627,"totalTokens":18081,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cacheWrite1h":7627,"reasoning":331},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792860765269,"responseId":"msg_011CgMQiZniNb3FUWHSgBF2z","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":14109,"thinkingLevel":"high"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_011MwUAGD7o5xVCaVdf9F1Qo","toolName":"probe","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Question posed — the turn ends here; the learner's graded answer arrives as this call's result."}],"details":null,"isError":false,"durationMs":0,"timestamp":1792860779382}]}

